Subject: [PATCH 11193/11362] Memory index drift: correct the record on what
 the live run showed

The spec and commit 115d8aeb30 said the live run demonstrated that moving
the description alone leaves a file DRIFTED. It did not: that edit never
applied, and the clear came from the tooling re-quote counting as a
description move under the raw hashing of that moment. The both-halves
rule is proven by unit tests and mutations M1/N3 only. Appended, not
rewritten. (First attempt was refused by a transient canonical-URL lint
state from a concurrent writer; the lint passes standalone.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 openspec/capabilities/research-harnesses/spec.md | 8 ++++++++
 ops/changelog.md                                 | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/openspec/capabilities/research-harnesses/spec.md b/openspec/capabilities/research-harnesses/spec.md
index 19a95a4f16..ce9c3d55a7 100644
--- a/openspec/capabilities/research-harnesses/spec.md
+++ b/openspec/capabilities/research-harnesses/spec.md
@@ -10252,6 +10252,14 @@ an anchor-context `description:` line silencing the reminder). Live first run: `
 next run`. Live end to end on the real directory: an append was reported DRIFTED (+10),
 moving the description alone left it DRIFTED, moving the index line as well cleared it.
 
+CORRECTION 2026-09-05 08:05Z, appended, not rewritten. The sentence above misreads the live run.
+The description edit in that sequence never applied (its text had been re-quoted by the tooling
+and the anchored replace found nothing), so the "still DRIFTED" reading was the unchanged state,
+and the flag then cleared because the re-quote counted as a description move under the raw
+hashing of that moment. The live run showed DRIFTED (+10) and then a clear; it did NOT show the
+both-halves rule. That rule is proven by the unit tests and mutations M1 and N3 only. The
+description was moved properly at 08:04Z and the live line reads `203 files, 0 drifted`.
+
